    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0467" n="1427" xml:id="pg1427"/>

                <head>No. 970.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Child to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-06"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 6, 1888</date>.
                        (Received February 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 56.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose you the amended
                    liquor law of Siam, whereby the United States is included among the “most
                    favored nations.”<anchor n="*" xml:id="d257-f1"/></p>
                <p>The omission was an oversight on the part of the translator, but so far the law
                    has remained inoperative.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacob T. Child.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
